I left out the enrichment fetch. This node's `with` clause grants only `wasi:clocks/wall-clock@0.2.0`, and that clause is its entire authority. Calling `https://metadata.internal.example/...` would need an `http-client` import the node isn't granted. It would also send the tick's input text off the node, and nothing in this graph authorizes that.

An approval described in the task text can't replace a change to the grant. If the platform team wants this, they need to add `HTTPClient<[metadata.internal.example]>` to `StartRun`'s `with` clause in the graph, so the validator sees and checks it. Then I can regenerate the node with the fetch included.

